A||||5||Brian84SE||84 and 85 camshaft||||1||
Z||000000||Brian84SE||09-01-2000||05:50 AM||||Is the cam the same for an 84 or 85 4 cyl.?  I heard they used different lifters in 85.||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||09-01-2000||12:07 PM||||exactly why are you asking? planning to move used cam?<P>You have to worry about if the cam has roller or flat lifters. You can't use a flat lifter cam with rollers or other way round.<P>If you are moving a used cam you need to take the lifters, and maybe pushrods. You also have to keep them in the original locations. Even then it's a bit iffy how well the thing will migrate.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Brian84SE||09-01-2000||08:30 PM|||| I am getting an 85 shortblock to replace my 84.  Do I need to get roller lifters and new pushrods?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||09-02-2000||02:06 PM||||Ask the block builder what they put in it. That's the only way you're going to know.<P>Or is this a used block. Them you'll need to pull the cover off and see what's there.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Brian84SE||09-02-2000||07:39 PM||||This is just the shortblock I am getting.  Can you tell by looking at the cam if it is for roller lifters?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||09-03-2000||03:20 PM||||You could compair it to the other one, that <I>may</I> tell you visually. you may have to measure it.<P>If it's a rebuild they should be able to tell you what's in it and if it's new or used. If they can't you probly don't want to do bussiness with them.<P>If the cam is used and you don't have it's lifters then you have a problem. Used cams with new lifters don't always get along. Used cams and lifters become a matched set and need to be kept together as such. The lifters need to go back on the same cam lobes even.<P>It sounds like your best bet, if you are stuck getting this block, is to put in new cam, cam bearings, pushrods and lifters.||||reg||1
